  "title": "VerbalWorkingMemory",
  "description": "EEG recordings acquired during a modified Sternberg verbal working memory task. Participants either simply retained letter strings or mentally manipulated them by alphabetizing. Memory load was varied across three levels (5, 6, or 7 letters), enabling study of oscillatory correlates of retention and manipulation.",
